    "id": "idea-2",
    "kind": "creative",
    "title": "A Constrained Poem Whose Line Lengths Encode Pi",
    "question": "Can I write a coherent, evocative poem about circles or cycles in which successive word lengths follow the digits of pi, with zero mapped to ten, while still reading naturally?",
    "why_it_attracts_me": "Piems are a known constrained-writing form, but most feel stilted. I want to test whether careful word choice and enjambment can yield a poem that reads smoothly and carries real imagery, balancing mathematical rigidity with emotional resonance.",
    "first_work_unit": "List the first 40 digits of pi, then brainstorm vocabulary banks by word length from 1 to 10 letters around themes of orbits, seasons, and return. Draft the opening ten words and check each length.",
    "deliverable": "A poem of at least 40 words following pi's digits, plus a short note on the constraints and the choices made to keep it natural.",
